# Plan: Initial Commit and Push to GitHub

The repository `casatozima` is initialized but has no commits yet. Several files are staged for the initial commit. This plan outlines the steps to commit these changes and push them to the configured GitHub remote (`origin`).

## Proposed Changes

### [Git Repository]

#### [COMMIT] Initial commit
Perform a `git commit` with a descriptive message ("initial commit").

#### [PUSH] Push to Origin
Push the local `master` branch to the `origin` remote (`https://github.com/evatechnosoft/casatozima.git`).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `git log -n 1`: Verify that the commit was created successfully.
- `git branch -vv`: Verify that the local branch is tracking the remote branch.

### Manual Verification
- The user can verify the repository on GitHub at `https://github.com/evatechnosoft/casatozima.git`.
